# logmaster — design decisions

## PWA and App structure

We want both PWA and native app versions (Capacitor for iOS, Android, and eventually macOS). This way we can add crew members without their having to install the app. The website/PWA remains the default entry point; native builds bundle `dist/client` and call the remote API via `VITE_PUBLIC_APP_URL`.

### Native app (Capacitor)

| Concern | Choice |
|---------|--------|
| Shell | Capacitor 8 — hybrid WebView over TanStack Start client bundle |
| Platforms | iOS + Android first; macOS via Xcode Mac target / Catalyst later |
| Background GPS | `@capacitor-community/background-geolocation` |
| Auto log entries | `HOURLY_LOG` with `data.autoGenerated` + `data.source: background-gps` while trip `IN_PROGRESS` |
| Notifications | `@capacitor/local-notifications` (Android 13+ permission for background GPS notification) |
| API origin | `src/lib/app-origin.ts` — native uses `VITE_PUBLIC_APP_URL`, web uses `window.location.origin` |

**Roadmap (native-only enhancements, minimal native code):**

1. **Background GPS recording** (v1) — auto-create editable log entries on interval / distance moved.
2. **Signal K** (v2) — WebSocket client in JS to ingest GPS, wind, heading, depth, water temp, AIS, engine RPM, battery voltage into log entry `data`.
3. **Bluetooth marine instruments** — prefer JS BLE plugins where possible (AIS, wind, Victron, etc.).
4. **Push + local notifications**, lock-screen widgets / Dynamic Island — native config + thin Capacitor plugins as needed.

Run `pnpm cap:sync` after `pnpm build`, then `pnpm cap:ios` or `pnpm cap:android`. For live reload during native dev: `CAP_DEV_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3020 pnpm cap:dev` (with `pnpm dev` running).

## Product

- **Sailing logbook PWA.** Users start trips, log events/notes/media locally, then sync when online.
- **Auth is optional for core use.** Sign-in enables cross-device sync; the app should work without connectivity or an account.
- **Scope is sailing/navigation logging only.** Do not reintroduce flight tracking, airline/airport catalogs, FR24, AirLabs, or similar.

## Stack

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| App | TanStack Start + React 19, file routes in `src/routes/` |
| API | Hono at `/api/*` (`src/server/hono.ts`) |
| Auth | Better Auth (`/api/auth/*`), Prisma adapter |
| DB | Postgres via Prisma (`prisma/schema.prisma`), shared **octacard** server, database **`logmaster`** |
| Jobs | pg-boss — currently `build_geo_features` only (`pnpm worker`) |
| Client state | Zustand (`src/stores/logbook.ts`) |
| Maps | MapLibre + server-side MapTiler proxy (`/api/map-tiles/…`) |
| PWA | vite-plugin-pwa, IndexedDB for offline tiles/geo (`src/lib/tile-idb.ts`) |

Dev server runs on **port 3020** (`pnpm dev`).

## Data model

Core entities: **Trip** → **LogEntry** → **Media**, plus Better Auth user tables and **Boat** → **BoatPhoto** (consortium-owned, photos in `S3_BUCKET_PHOTOS`).

- Log entries use typed events (`SAILS_UP`, `ANCHOR_DROPPED`, `NOTE`, `PHOTO`, etc.) — see `src/domain/logbook.ts`.
- Entries carry `synced` and soft-delete (`deleted`) flags for offline sync.
- Domain types live in `src/domain/`; keep UI and API aligned with these types.

## Permissions

**Boats and orgs are separate.** A personal boat is owned via `Boat.userId` with its own photos and documents. An **org** is an optional group for syndicate operations: shared org documents, contacts, members, scheduling context, and one or more attached boats.

- **Boat access:** creator (`userId`) has full access; **share owners** get member-level boat/trip access; if the boat is attached to an org, org members also get access per role.
- **Org access:** membership roles only — not implied by boat ownership alone. Attach a boat to an org explicitly via `/api/orgs/:id/boats`.
- **`createdByUserId`** on an org is audit/display only — it does not gate access.
- **Roles:** `OWNER`, `ADMIN`, `MEMBER`, `VIEWER` on org membership — mapped to privileges in `src/server/permissions/`.
- **Boat shares:** each boat has a fixed `shareCount`. Shares are ordered by `sequence` (0-based, stable display order for scheduling). Each share can have multiple owners who split that share equally. Shares live on the boat; they do not require an org.
- **Share slots:** every share index `0 … shareCount-1` exists as a row even when unassigned, so scheduling UIs stay consistent.
- **Visibility** on the org: `PRIVATE` (members only), `UNLISTED` (share link/token), `PUBLIC` (discoverable — future).
- **Boat log access:** trip creator (`Trip.userId`) or anyone with boat access (owner, share owner, org member for attached boats) via `Trip.boatId`.
- **Routes** follow the same pattern: creator-owned, with boat-linked routes visible to users with boat access.
- **Inheritance:** photos, documents, log entries, and other child resources inherit access from their container (boat or trip via boat).
- **Crew vs org:** crew roster (`CrewMember`) is for trip logging UX. Accepting a crew invite adds org `MEMBER` only when the inviter has boats attached to an org. Adding a share owner grants org membership only when the boat is attached to an org.
- **Boat members vs org:** joining an org-attached boat (invite accept or direct add) auto-adds org `MEMBER` as a separate `ConsortiumMember` record. Attaching a boat to an org backfills org membership for existing boat members. Org membership is not auto-removed when boat membership ends — remove from org manually after removing from all org boats.
- **Org member removal:** cannot remove an org member while they still have a `BoatMember` row on any boat attached to that org.
- **API:** `/api/orgs/…` for org management; `/api/boats/:id/shares` for share structure and owners; authorization checks via `canAccess()` in route handlers.

## Offline-first behaviour

1. **Write locally first** (Zustand + IndexedDB/local storage patterns in the logbook store).
2. **Sync in background** when `online` — do not block UI on network calls.
3. **Surface sync state** in the UI (unsynced counts, badges) without modal noise.

## API conventions

- Logbook routes: `/api/logbook/…` (`src/server/routes/logbook.ts`) — auth required; scoped by boat/org access.
- Boats routes: `/api/boats/…` (`src/server/routes/boats.ts`) — auth required; boat ownership/shares/org membership; photo bytes at `/api/boats/photos/:id/content`.
- Org routes: `/api/orgs/…` (`src/server/routes/consortia.ts`) — member list, add, role change, remove.
- Admin routes: `/api/admin/…` (pg-boss, countries/geo imports).
- Health check: `/api/health`.
- Use Hono sub-routers; mount new domains on `src/server/hono.ts`.

## UI & theming

- **Apple News–inspired editorial layout:** clean white/black surfaces, large imagery, section titles in brand red.
- **Brand red** from the sail logo (`--brand`, `--brand-hover`, `--brand-muted`) — use for section titles (`.brand-title`), menu emphasis, and the wordmark; keep body text monochrome.
- Logo asset: `/logmaster_logo_transparent.png` in header and auth screens.
- Theme tokens in `src/styles.css`:

  - Brand: `--brand`, `--brand-hover`, `--brand-muted`
  - Text: `--sea-ink`, `--sea-ink-soft`
  - Surfaces: `--bg-base`, `--panel`, `--surface-strong`, `--chip-bg`
  - Primary actions: `--btn-bg`, `--btn-text`
  - Borders: `--line`, `--panel-border`

- Boats list (`/boats`): large cover image per boat, name underneath (Apple News carousel/card pattern).
- Theme toggle supports light / dark / system via `data-theme` + `.dark` class.
- Display headings: Fraunces (`display-title`); body: Manrope.

## Tooling

- **Biome** for formatting (`pnpm format`), **ESLint** for linting (`pnpm lint`).
- **Vitest** for tests.
- Prisma migrations in `prisma/migrations/` — use `pnpm db:migrate`, not ad-hoc SQL.
- Path alias: `#/*` → `./src/*`.

## Code style (agents)

- Minimize scope; match existing patterns in neighbouring files.
- No over-abstraction; comments only for non-obvious business logic.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`); keep `.env.example` in sync when adding env vars.

## Environment

- `DATABASE_URL` → octacard Postgres on `localhost:5432`, database `logmaster`.
- `BETTER_AUTH_URL` must match the browser origin (including port).
- MapTiler key via `VITE_MAPTILER_API_KEY` (server reads env at runtime for tile proxy).
